1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,376
When a winter storm cut Maeve Brennan's power, \ the first person to check on her \ was not a paid caregiver \ but a neighbor \ she had met days earlier.
当一场冬季暴风雪切断了梅芙·布伦南家的电源时， \ 第一个前去探望她的人 \ 并不是花钱雇来的护工， \ 而是一位邻居， \ 她几天前刚刚认识的。

2
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:16,142
The two women had been linked to each other \ through a local time bank, \ a scheme matching households needing help \ with those able to give it.
这两位女性被联系在了一起， \ 通过当地一家“时间银行”， \ 一个将需要帮助的家庭 \ 与能够提供帮助的人进行匹配的项目。

3
00:00:16,492 --> 00:00:21,556
Every hour spent helping others \ earns a credit \ that can be saved and spent later.
帮助他人所花费的每个小时， \ 都能赚取一个时间积分/额度， \ 能够被存起来并在日后消费使用。

4
00:00:21,906 --> 00:00:24,450
Time banks \ are nothing new.
时间银行 \ 并不是什么新鲜事。

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:33,032
The idea originated in Japan in the 1970s, \ when young mothers wanted to share childcare, \ and has since spread worldwide.
这一构想于20世纪70年代起源于日本， \ 当时年轻母亲们希望分担育儿， \ 自那以后便在全世界传播开来。

6
00:00:33,382 --> 00:00:42,262
What is novel about the modern version \ is its software: \ an application now handles the matching and reminders \ once left to exhausted volunteers.
现代版本的新颖之处 \ 在于其软件： \ 一款应用程序如今处理匹配和提醒事项， \ 曾经全留给精疲力竭的志愿者们承担。

7
00:00:42,612 --> 00:00:47,604
Such schemes, supporters argue, \ offer more than practical help.
支持者主张，此类方案 \ 所提供的远不止实际的帮助。

8
00:00:47,954 --> 00:01:03,314
Since nobody is paid, \ the exchange feels more like an act of neighborliness \ than a commercial transaction; \ and since time, not money, is the measure of worth, \ members describe a fresh sense of belonging, \ of being part of a place \ rather than merely passing through it.
由于没有人拿取报酬， \ 这种互助感觉更像是一种睦邻行为， \ 而非一场商业交易； \ 并且由于时间而非金钱是价值的衡量标准， \ 成员们描述了一种全新的归属感， \ 真正成为一个地方的一部分， \ 而非仅仅是这里的过客。

9
00:01:03,664 --> 00:01:12,208
Dutch researchers tracking 400 households \ found participants reported substantially higher levels of trust \ in their neighbors \ than non-members did.
跟踪了400个家庭的荷兰研究人员 \ 发现参与者报告了明显大幅更高的信任水平， \ 对他们的邻居， \ 相比非成员而言。

10
00:01:12,558 --> 00:01:15,150
Not everyone \ is convinced.
并非所有人 \ 都对此信服。

11
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:23,108
Critics note \ that reliable volunteers are still notoriously hard to find, \ and that most work falls on a few organizers.
批评人士指出， \ 可靠的志愿者依然是出名地难找， \ 并且大部分工作落在了少数几个组织者身上。

12
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:31,090
Fairness is another concern: \ members in remote areas \ may spend so long traveling \ that the scheme stops being convenient.
公平性是另一个关切点： \ 偏远地区的成员 \ 可能在路上花费如此多的时间， \ 以至于该方案不再显得便利。

13
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:42,648
Even so, Brennan, 78, says her life has changed: \ "I used to go whole days without speaking to anyone. \ Now I know somebody will notice \ if I don't appear."
即便如此，78岁的布伦南说她的生活改变了： \ “我过去常常一整天不跟任何人说话。 \ 现在我知道有人会察觉到， \ 如果我没有露面的话。”
